    "profile_text": {
        "body": "Aurora Innovation, Inc. is a public company headquartered in Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania, with the ticker AUR and the website aurora.tech. According to its own site, the company works on self-driving freight powered by the Aurora Driver, which it describes as built with cutting-edge hardware and software backed by verifiable AI and as a way to integrate autonomy into a customer's fleet. The company frames its aim as delivering self-driving technology safely, quickly, and broadly.\n\nThe site carries quotes from partners rather than named executives. One quote describes early results of a pilot program with Aurora, including autonomous hauling of freight between Fort Worth and El Paso, and a hybrid model combining Werner professional drivers with the Aurora Driver. Another says the Aurora Driver is integrated into the Volvo VNL Autonomous. A further quote states that freight volumes are projected to grow five fold between 2010 and 2050, and another cites consistent performance of the self-driving system over millions of autonomous miles and compares the Aurora Driver's intended performance to that of today's CDL drivers.\n\nThe company's record shows a legal exposure entry for Pennsylvania with a count of 154. No lawsuits, products, or MCP servers are listed for it. Its SEC central index key is 0001828108.",
